      "hook": "Lady Harrington taunts, 'Imagine Juliana seeing this,' followed by Lord Harrington's cold threat: 'She won't be seeing anything for long.'",
      "cliffhanger": "The Elder Nobleman declares with a sinister smile that the 'witch will be dead' by sunset.",
      "why": "Starts immediately with cruel dialogue about execution rather than establishing shots, creating immediate stakes and villainy.",
      "context_gap": "Strangers won't know who Juliana is or why she is called a witch without prior context."
    },
    {
      "title": "The Bride's Arrival",
      "start_block": "B042",
      "end_block": "B051",
      "hook": "Catherine appears in a breathtaking bridal gown as Rupert stares in awe, while Lady Harrington whispers, 'She looks like a queen.'",
      "cliffhanger": "Catherine smugly insults Rupert, saying he looks better in silk than as an 'ignored cousin,' ending on their triumphant smiles.",
      "why": "Visual spectacle of the bride combined with the villainous dialogue creates a strong hook and ends on a character moment rather than action resolution.",
      "context_gap": "Viewers may not understand the significance of the 'ignored cousin' insult or the full scope of the conspiracy."
    },
    {
      "title": "Sealed for Death",
      "start_block": "B029",
      "end_block": "B036",
      "hook": "An elder nobleman sternly asks if all entrances are covered, receiving confirmation that 'Every one' is sealed.",
      "cliffhanger": "The nobleman states ruthlessly, 'By sunset, Ashburgh will have its new Duke and Duchess,' implying a usurpation.",
      "why": "High tension dialogue about sealing exits creates immediate suspense about entrapment and betrayal.",
      "context_gap": "Without knowing the characters, viewers might not realize the 'new Duke' refers to the usurper Rupert and the 'witch' refers to Juliana."
    }
  ],
